#. type: Plain text
#: debian-bookworm
msgid ""
"The B<difftime>()  function returns the number of seconds elapsed between "
"time I<time1> and time I<time0>, represented as a I<double>.  Each of the "
"times is specified in calendar time, which means its value is a measurement "
"(in seconds) relative to the Epoch, 1970-01-01 00:00:00 +0000 (UTC)."
msgstr ""
"La fonction B<difftime>() renvoie le nombre de secondes écoulées entre les "
"instants I<time1> et I<time0> au format I<double>. Les deux paramètres de "
"temps sont de type calendrier, ce qui représente le temps écoulé depuis "
"l'époque, 1er janvier 1970 à 00:00:00 (UTC)."

#. type: Plain text
#: debian-bookworm
msgid "POSIX.1-2001, POSIX.1-2008, C99, SVr4, 4.3BSD."
msgstr "POSIX.1-2001, POSIX.1-2008, C99, SVr4, 4.3BSD."

#. type: SH
#: debian-bookworm
#, no-wrap
msgid "NOTES"
msgstr "NOTES"

#. type: Plain text
#: debian-bookworm
msgid ""
"On a POSIX system, I<time_t> is an arithmetic type, and one could just define"
msgstr ""
"Sur un système POSIX, I<time_t> est un type arithmétique, et on peut définir "
"directement"

#. type: Plain text
#: debian-bookworm
#, no-wrap
msgid "#define difftime(t1,t0) (double)(t1 - t0)\n"
msgstr "#define difftime(t1,t0) (double)(t1 - t0)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: debian-bookworm
msgid "when the possible overflow in the subtraction is not a concern."
msgstr "si les risques de débordement ne sont pas gênants."

